idence":"Net debt/EBITDA -0.3"},{"label":"Not diluting shareholders","ok":false,"evidence":"Diluted share count +1.1% YoY"},{"label":"Analyst estimates moving higher","ok":null,"evidence":"Estimate-revision feed not connected (Phase 2)"},{"label":"Management guidance increasing","ok":null,"evidence":"Earnings Intelligence Engine not built (Phase 2)"}],"thesis":"Micron Technology (MU) screens at opportunity 75.0 with an expectations gap of 28.0. Reality 84.0 reflects +167.0% TTM revenue growth, +65.6% operating margin and +74.5% ROIC; pricing 56.0 reflects a fair multiple and strong price momentum. Primary theme exposure: AI Infrastructure (trend 59.0). Macro fit for Technology in a Goldilocks regime is 54.0/100.","market_expectation":{"summary":"Priced roughly in line with its own history and peers; the market expects the current trajectory to continue.","evidence":["EV/Sales 12.7x (78.0th pct of own 5y range)","P/E 23x (18.0th pct of own history)","FCF yield 2.2%","PEG 0.0","12m return +550%, -12% from 52w high"]},"what_market_misses":["Reality (84.0) is running ahead of what is priced (56.0): an expectations gap of +28 pts.","Revenue growth is accelerating (+167.0% TTM, +81.4 pts) while the multiple has not re-rated.","Operating leverage is showing up in margins faster than in the valuation."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (roughly 90 days after the last filing on 2026-06-25)","AI Infrastructure: evidence that 'GPU supply, power availability, cooling, network bandwidth' is easing via Accelerators, optical/electrical interconnect, HBM memory, liquid cooling, on-site power","Edge AI: evidence that 'Power-efficient silicon, on-device memory' is easing via NPUs in phones/PCs/cars, low-power memory","Continued rotation into Technology"],"risks":["No engine-flagged risks; standard execution and macro risk apply."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 117% (currently 167.0%)","ROIC falls below 56% (currently 74.5%)","Operating margin YoY change falls below -2.0 pts (currently +43.0 pts)","Technology rotation score stays below -30 for two consecutive weeks (currently +68)","Adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55%","Price closes >10% below its 200-day average with negative relative strength","AI Infrastructure theme trend drops below 45 (currently 59.0)"],"break_rules":[{"id":"revenue_growth","label":"TTM revenue growth","metric":"revenue_growth","op":"<","threshold":1.1689,"current":1.6698},{"id":"roic","label":"ROIC","metric":"roic","op":"<","threshold":0.5586,"current":0.7448},{"id":"margin","label":"Operating margin change YoY","metric":"operating_margin_change","op":"<","threshold":-0.02,"current":0.4303681649003577},{"id":"rotation","label":"Technology rotation score","metric":"sector_rotation","op":"<","threshold":-30,"consecutive_weeks":2,"current":68.0},{"id":"regime","label":"P(Stagflation)+P(Contraction)","metric":"adverse_regime_prob","op":">","threshold":55,"current":49.900000000000006},{"id":"trend","label":"Distance from 200dma","metric":"dist_200dma","op":"<","threshold":-10,"and_negative_rs":true,"current":58.2},{"id":"theme","label":"AI Infrastructure theme trend","metric":"theme_trend","theme_id":"ai-infrastructure","op":"<","threshold":45,"current":59.0}],"narrative_note":"Narrative from the last 7 morning briefs' theme signals (exposure-weighted).","llm_enriched":true,"theme_exposures":[{"theme_id":"ai-infrastructure","theme":"AI Infrastructure","weight":0.7,"order":1,"effective":0.7},{"theme_id":"edge-ai","theme":"Edge AI","weight":0.2,"order":2,"effective":0.12}],"llm":{"thesis":"Micron is in the middle of an AI-memory supercycle where TTM revenue growth has accelerated to +167% and operating margin has expanded over 43 points YoY, yet the stock trades at only the 78th percentile of its own 5-year EV/Sales range and the 18th percentile on P/E - well below where comparable growth/margin inflections have historically re-rated. Capital is rotating hard into Technology (+68 sector score) and price action confirms it (above all key moving averages, RSI 60, positive MACD), but the stock is still 12% off its 52-week high after a historic 550% 12-month run, suggesting the market has priced strong momentum without fully crediting the magnitude of the fundamental re-rating. The 28-point expectations gap (reality 84 vs priced 56) is the core edge: memory pricing/HBM demand strength appears to be outrunning consensus multiples. This is a quality compounder (ROIC 74.5%, net debt negative, near-zero dilution) riding the AI infrastructure buildout, not a story stock. The main offset is cyclicality risk inherent to memory markets and a theme-trend reading (59) that is strong but not yet accelerating further.","fundamental_read":"Revenue growth has accelerated from +85.5% to +167% TTM with operating margin expanding to 65.6% (+4,304 bps YoY) and ROIC at 74.5%, reflecting severe HBM/DRAM pricing tightness flowing through to the P&L. FCF grew nearly 13x to a 29% margin despite heavy capex ($25.3B), and the balance sheet is net-cash (-0.3x net debt/EBITDA) with interest coverage over 250x. Dilution is minimal (+1.1% YoY) and buybacks/dividends remain modest relative to cash generation, indicating capital is being redeployed into capacity rather than returned to shareholders.","technical_read":"Price sits well above its 20/50/200-day averages in a confirmed uptrend (50>200), with RSI at 60 and positive MACD signaling continued but non-overbought momentum. The stock is 12.2% off its 52-week high after a +215% six-month and +550% twelve-month move, suggesting a pause/consolidation within an intact uptrend rather than a breakdown.","market_expectation":"Valuation at 78th percentile EV/Sales but only 18th percentile P/E and a PEG near zero implies the market expects the current earnings trajectory to persist near-term but is not yet pricing durable structural re-rating; momentum traders are rewarding the move while fundamental multiples remain historically muted relative to the magnitude of margin/ROIC expansion.","what_market_misses":["Reality score (84) materially exceeds priced score (56), a 28-point gap that historically closes via further re-rating or continued earnings beats.","Margin and ROIC expansion (operating margin +4,304 bps YoY, ROIC 74.5%) is structural to the AI memory cycle (HBM) but valuation multiples (P/E 18th percentile) still reflect pre-cycle skepticism about durability.","Theme exposure trend (59-60) is solid but engine flags it as 'not strengthening further,' implying the market may be underpricing a second leg if AI infrastructure capex continues to broaden beyond current assumptions."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly earnings report (~90 days post 2026-06-25 filing) to confirm continued revenue/margin acceleration","Evidence that GPU/power/cooling/interconnect bottlenecks are easing, which would validate sustained HBM and memory demand from AI infrastructure buildout","Edge AI adoption (NPUs in phones/PCs/cars) driving incremental low-power memory demand","Continued capital rotation into Technology sector (currently +68 rotation score)"],"risks":["Memory is historically cyclical; a pricing downturn or oversupply could reverse margin/ROIC gains quickly","No engine-flagged idiosyncratic risks were identified, so execution and macro risk are the primary residual concerns","Regime probabilities are split nearly evenly across Goldilocks/Reflation/Stagflation/Contraction (~22-28% each), leaving macro fragility that could pressure the Technology sector rotation that currently supports the stock","Valuation, while below historical EV/Sales percentile extremes, is still elevated on an absolute P/FCF basis (44.7x) and FCF yield is low (2.2%), limiting margin of safety if growth decelerates"],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 117% (from 167%)","ROIC falls below 56% (from 74.5%)","Operating margin YoY change turns negative beyond -2.0 pts (from +43.0 pts)","Technolog